## Local Context

If `~/.codex/machine.md` exists, read it for machine-local notes. It is intentionally
not synchronized. Discover the current home directory, operating system, shell,
available tools, and repository paths instead of assuming a particular machine.

## Attribution

Do not add AI co-author trailers, generated-by text, or session links to commits or
pull/merge requests unless I explicitly ask for them.

## RTK

When installed, RTK's Codex hook rewrites supported shell commands to reduce output.
Use `rtk gain` for statistics and `rtk proxy <command>` when unfiltered output is needed.
Do not assume Claude's hook configuration applies to Codex.

## Context7

For external library/framework documentation, use Context7 when it is available.
